Changes made to ProtoMotions
----------------------------
This repository starts from ProtoMotions at commit a87d2f3 (2026-05-03) and changes it as
follows, as required by section 4(b) of the Apache License, Version 2.0:

* Reduced to the Isaac Gym simulator and the smpl_mor robot. The code for the other
  simulators, the other robots, the examples and the documentation was removed. The
  configuration classes of the other simulators are kept so that saved checkpoints
  still load.
* Added support for many body shapes in one training run: the smpl_mor robot (128 SMPL
  body shapes), morphology-aware environments and observations, and the matching
  changes to the agent, environment, simulator and utility code.
* Added streamed clip sampling (GlobalClipPool and MotionLibPool), the validation and
  test evaluators, the experiment files for the paper, and the tools for reference
  generation, refinement, evaluation and analysis.

44 files that come from ProtoMotions are modified and 38 files are new;
MODIFICATIONS.md lists them. The other 83 files that come from ProtoMotions are
unchanged.

Third-party material
--------------------
SMPL body models. The 130 files in protomotions/data/assets/mjcf/smpl_mor/ (128 MJCF body
files, assets.yaml and physics_features.pt) and the 258 files in
protomotions/data/assets/mjcf/smpl_mor_unseen_inside/ and smpl_mor_unseen_outside/ (128 MJCF
body files and assets.yaml in each) are derived from the SMPL body model of the Max
Planck Institute for Intelligent Systems and the Max-Planck-Gesellschaft zur Förderung der
Wissenschaften e.V. (https://smpl.is.tue.mpg.de/). They are not covered by the Apache License
of this repository. They are made available with attribution under the terms of the SMPL-Body
license, the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(https://smpl.is.tue.mpg.de/bodylicense.html, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
Changes made: each MJCF file describes one body shape (one SMPL shape vector, written out with
SMPLSim) as a MuJoCo model of box, capsule and sphere geometries with densities, joints and
joint limits for physics simulation. The files contain no mesh, no shape blendshapes and no
SMPL model files. Creating new bodies requires the SMPL model files and the SMPL Model License
(non-commercial research), which are not included. If you use these files, please cite:
M. Loper, N. Mahmood, J. Romero, G. Pons-Moll and M. J. Black, "SMPL: A Skinned Multi-Person
Linear Model", ACM Transactions on Graphics 34(6), 248:1-248:16, 2015.

Shape coefficients. protomotions/data/assets/all_betas.pt holds the 64 shape coefficient vectors
sampled for this work (NumPy seed 46). It is covered by the Apache License. The shape vector of
every body, including those of the two unseen panels, is also listed in its assets.yaml.

Clip identifiers. data/preprocessing/valid_ids_sorted_by_difficulty.txt and data/splits/ list
HumanML3D clip identifiers with difficulty scores and split hashes. No motion data is included;
the motions remain under the AMASS (Max-Planck) and HumanML3D terms.

SMPL model files, AMASS, HumanML3D, HUMOS and Isaac Gym are not part of this repository and
remain under their own terms.
